Reviewed `src/blog/people/drafts/Stavros-Halkias.md` and appended a `FRESH EYES REVIEW` block at the bottom. No body edits.

**The two biggest flags:**

1. **The weight is the loudest fact about him and the draft ducks it.** The persona setup is "fat, filthy," the Netflix hour is called *Fat Rascal*, and the tour he's on right now is called **The Dreamboat Tour** — the joke being that the fat guy became a sex symbol. He hit 290 lbs on that tour. All of it lives in one clause inside the Rabbit Hole. That's also the sharpest live contradiction the piece has available: a Seven whose brand is bottomless appetite deliberately rationing the one appetite the audience pays to watch.

2. **Two things missing outright.** He co-wrote, produced and starred in *Let's Start a Cult* (2024, theatrical → Hulu) — the one project he authored rather than was cast in, and the best evidence for the ownership read the Rabbit Hole is arguing. And he campaigned for Zohran Mamdani, which is the concrete receipt the carveout section asserts but never shows.

Also worth knowing before the next pass: the `$30,000` runs six times in the body, and the Rabbit Hole re-quotes four lines already used verbatim earlier. The receipt table, the green-card spine, and the closing rug pair are the parts to protect.

Sources: [Baltimore Magazine](https://www.baltimoremagazine.com/section/artsentertainment/stavros-halkias-comedian-actor-podcaster-profile-greektown-baltimore-native-rise-to-fame/), [Let's Start a Cult (Wikipedia)](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Let's_Start_a_Cult), [IndieWire interview](https://www.indiewire.com/features/interviews/stavros-halkias-interview-lets-start-a-cult-1235057960/), [Slate](https://slate.com/culture/2025/10/stavros-halkias-stavvy-bugonia-comedian-cum-town-interview.html)
